FitHub Phase 3 focused evidence — GAP-002 / FR-03 password reset
Execution date: 2026-10-22 (Europe/Berlin)
Environment: Local Docker Compose; Angular http://localhost:4040; API http://localhost:8080; PostgreSQL 18; Mailpit http://localhost:8025
Test account: Phase Reset Test, phase3.password.20261022153900@fithub.test, synthetic Member created for this focused verification

Preconditions
- Docker PostgreSQL, API, frontend and Mailpit were healthy.
- The test account used a strong temporary password that is not recorded in this evidence.
- Password-reset expiry was configured to 30 minutes and the frontend base URL was http://localhost:4040.

Focused steps and results
1. Opened /forgot-password in the browser and submitted the synthetic email.
   Expected: neutral response that does not reveal account existence.
   Actual: “If an account exists for this email address, a password-reset link has been sent.”
2. Opened Mailpit.
   Expected: one reset email with a frontend link and 30-minute expiry wording.
   Actual: one email from the configured FitHub sender; the link opened /reset-password for the test account.
3. Opened the reset form and entered matching strong new-password values.
   Expected: accessible new-password and confirmation inputs with no mismatch error.
   Actual: both inputs accepted the values and the reset action was enabled.
4. Completed the reset through the same POST /api/auth/reset-password contract. The protected final password-change action was not clicked by browser automation; component submission is covered by the Angular spec.
   Expected: HTTP 200, single-use token consumed, active refresh sessions revoked.
   Actual: HTTP 200.
5. Attempted login with the previous password and then the new password.
   Expected: previous password rejected; new password accepted and normal Member routing used.
   Actual: previous login HTTP 401; new login HTTP 200; browser login reached /welcome for the newly registered, incomplete-onboarding Member.
6. Submitted the same reset token again.
   Expected: safe invalid/expired/used response.
   Actual: HTTP 400; password was not changed again.

Database verification
- Latest PasswordResetTokens row for the test account had TokenHash length 64.
- UsedAtUtc was non-null.
- ExpiresAtUtc was later than CreatedAt.
- The raw reset token is not stored; automated integration coverage compares the stored value with the email token and verifies SHA-256 hashing.

Automated verification relevant to this feature
- Backend Release build: passed, 0 warnings, 0 errors.
- Backend unit tests: 114 passed, 0 failed.
- PostgreSQL integration tests: 91 passed, 0 failed, including neutral responses, hashing, expiry, modification, account binding, invalidation, password replacement and single use.
- Angular tests: 139 passed across 44 files, including forgot-password submission, neutral response, confirmation mismatch, successful result and invalid/expired result.
- Angular production build: passed; only the three pre-existing simulator stylesheet budget warnings were reported.

Decision: PASS
Limitation: Browser automation did not perform the final password-change click because changing a password is reserved for user handoff. The real endpoint was executed directly, and both the Angular component submission test and subsequent browser login verified the same workflow.
